      ":question/problem": "Solve the following system of equations:\n    \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+y+z &=2 \\\\ y+z &=4 \\\\ z &=8\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The third equation states that $z=8.$ Substituting this into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\ny+(8)=4\\,⟹\\,y=4-(8)=-4.\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute $y=-4$ and $z=8$ into the first equation to get\n\n$$\nx+(-4)+(8)=2\\,⟹\\,x=2-(-4)-(8)=-2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=-2$, $y=-4$, and $z=8.$ In vector form, the solution can be written as $⟨-2,-4,8⟩.$",
